我的朋友和我的朋友，我们俩，对我们来说在艺术上意义重大的人，罗布·莱纳和他的妻子米歇尔，非常悲惨地去世了，就在我们录制这段视频的几天前。

00:44:29.150 --> 00:45:00.990
And I just wanted to kind of just have a couple of words about what his movies meant to both of us, just personally, and I just posted something on Instagram about this, but Rob cast me in a pilot for NBC called Everyday Life in 2003 or four, I can't remember, and the pilot was never picked up, but he directed it, he played my dad, Mercedes, who played my mom, it's about a family of therapists all live and work in the same brownstone.
我只是想简单谈谈他的电影对我们俩的意义，就我个人而言，我刚刚在 Instagram 上发布了一些相关内容，但罗布在 2003 年或四年前让我出演了 NBC 的一部名为《日常生活》的试播集，我记不清了，试播集一直没有被接拍，但他导演了这部片子，他扮演了我的父亲梅赛德斯，谁扮演了我的妈妈，这是关于一个家庭治疗师的故事，他们都在同一个上流社会生活和工作。

00:45:00.990 --> 00:45:05.643
And it was all improvised and it was really wild and really fun.
这一切都是即兴创作的，非常狂野，非常有趣。

00:45:05.643 --> 00:45:18.728
And I got to know Rob and we had lunch over the years many times and he screened a cut of my second movie at his house with his wife and they gave me such beautiful feedback on it.
我认识了罗布，多年来我们多次共进午餐，他和他的妻子在他家里放映了我的第二部电影的剪辑，他们给了我非常好的反馈。

00:45:18.728 --> 00:45:23.235
And he was just a lovely, generous, passionate, beautiful man.
他是一个可爱、慷慨、热情、美丽的男人。

00:45:23.235 --> 00:45:26.797
And he also made some of the greatest films ever.
他还制作了一些有史以来最伟大的电影。

00:45:26.797 --> 00:45:30.941
I mean, truly like Pantheon films, you know, stand by me.
我的意思是，真的像万神殿电影一样，你知道，支持我。

00:45:30.941 --> 00:45:37.120
This is Spinal Tap, the Princess Bride, when Harry Met Sally, Misery, a few good men.
这是《脊椎泰普》，《公主新娘》，当哈利遇到莎莉、米塞里和几个好男人时。

00:45:37.120 --> 00:45:41.699
Like, you can't believe that one director directed all of this.
就像，你无法相信一位导演导演了这一切。

00:45:41.699 --> 00:45:42.726
It's astonishing.
真是令人惊讶。

00:45:42.726 --> 00:45:44.659
It's an astonishing achievement.
这是一个令人惊讶的成就。

00:45:44.659 --> 00:45:45.819
Who else could do that?
还有谁能做到这一点？

00:45:45.819 --> 00:45:46.979
I don't know any of it.
我什么都不知道。

00:45:46.980 --> 00:45:47.820
It's the range of it.
这是它的范围。

00:45:47.820 --> 00:45:50.519
And it was in the span of a few years.
而且这只是几年的时间。

00:45:50.519 --> 00:45:57.280
Like he had a run that is just among the all time creative runs in the history of film.
就像他的一次奔跑只是电影史上最富有创意的奔跑之一。

00:45:57.280 --> 00:45:59.619
I mean, it stands next to any other body.
我的意思是，它站在任何其他身体旁边。

00:45:59.619 --> 00:46:05.039
So what creative DNA do you think is Reiner-esque that found its way into how I met your mother?
那么你认为莱纳式的创意 DNA 融入到了我与你母亲的邂逅中？

00:46:05.039 --> 00:46:13.900
I think you can make an argument that how I met your mother is essentially when Harry Metzali meets, stand by me meets the Princess Bride.
我想你可以说我是如何遇见你母亲的，本质上就是哈利·梅扎利遇见了，站在我身边遇见了公主新娘。

00:46:13.900 --> 00:46:19.619
Because when Harry Metzali is the gold standard New York romantic comedy, right?
因为当哈利·梅扎利成为纽约浪漫喜剧的黄金标准时，对吗？

00:46:19.619 --> 00:46:23.340
I mean, there's just like, it's just untouchable.
我的意思是，就像，它是不可触碰的。

00:46:23.340 --> 00:46:26.980
And even within that movie, there is the framework of it's a story kind of being told.
即使在那部电影中，也有一个讲述故事的框架。

00:46:26.980 --> 00:46:34.500
All those couples you see, interspersed with, obviously Nora Afran wrote it beautifully, but I know she developed that whole project with Rob so collaboratively.
你看到的所有那些情侣，显然诺拉·阿夫兰（Nora Afran）写得很漂亮，但我知道她和罗布（Rob）如此合作地开发了整个项目。

00:46:34.500 --> 00:47:26.098
And then in like the Princess Bride, that idea of a story being told and popping in and out of the story, a story being told to a child by an older, wiser person and pop jumping in and out of the story, if you put that together with when Harry Met Sally, that's basically how I met your mother and stand by me having again that future narrator kind of making sense of, in that case, childhood, but remembering this beautiful chapter of his life that he's trying to capture as an adult in his middle age, who's played beautifully by Richard Dreyfus in the movie, God damn, that's how your mother all of those things are how much mother and then like the musical comedy piece like when Carter and I would write those Robin Sparkle songs what I would always look to was this is Spinal Tap because the songs that they did for the Spinal Tap they wrote them to be good songs.
然后就像《公主新娘》一样，一个故事被讲述，然后在故事中突然出现，一个由一个年长、更聪明的人给一个孩子讲的故事，然后在故事中跳进跳出，如果你把它和《哈利遇到莎莉》放在一起，这基本上就是我遇见你母亲的方式，并再次支持我，让未来的叙述者有点理解，在这种情况下，童年，但记住他生命中这一美丽的篇章，他在成年后试图捕捉到这一章理查德·德雷福斯 (Richard Dreyfus) 在电影《天杀的，这就是你的母亲》中扮演的非常漂亮的年龄，这就是你母亲的样子，所有这些事情都是多么母亲，然后喜欢音乐喜剧片，就像卡特和我写那些罗宾·斯帕克尔的歌一样，我一直关注的是《Spinal Tap》，因为他们为《Spinal Tap》写的歌曲都是好歌。

00:47:26.098 --> 00:47:28.174
Those are really really good songs.
这些都是非常非常好的歌曲。

00:47:28.174 --> 00:47:51.779
They were so deadpan about what that movie was that they said the songs will be absurd but we're also going to make them great and there's something about, Reiner is like just control of tone, even within these incredibly diverse projects that he just knows what these things are, talk about these other DNA, like the DNA of those things, every molecule of those movies knows what movie they're in.
他们对那部电影的内容如此面无表情，以至于他们说这些歌曲会很荒谬，但我们也会让它们变得很棒，而且有一些东西，莱纳就像是对音调的控制，即使在这些令人难以置信的多样化项目中，他也知道这些东西是什么，谈论这些其他的DNA，就像那些东西的DNA一样，这些电影的每个分子都知道它们在哪部电影中。

00:47:51.779 --> 00:47:55.515
And that is coming through the singular vision of Ralph Reiner.
这是通过拉尔夫·雷纳 (Ralph Reiner) 的独特愿景实现的。

00:47:55.515 --> 00:47:56.227
I loved him.
我爱他。

00:47:56.227 --> 00:47:57.176
I love his work.
我喜欢他的工作。

00:47:57.176 --> 00:47:58.599
I never got to meet him.
我一直没能见到他。

00:47:58.599 --> 00:48:01.980
I feel like I lost a friend and I never even met the man.
我觉得我失去了一个朋友，而我什至从未见过这个人。

00:48:01.980 --> 00:48:08.860
And boy, his influence on everything and how much mother included is just beyond measure, he's just a brilliant man.
男孩，他对一切的影响以及母亲的影响是无法估量的，他是一个才华横溢的人。

00:48:08.860 --> 00:48:18.385
Yeah, and I think also if you could distill or boil down what is a director's job, it's to make sure everyone's in the same movie that there's a kind of...
是的，我认为如果你可以提炼或归结什么是导演的工作，那就是确保每个人都在同一部电影中，有一种......

00:48:18.385 --> 00:48:24.347
I read this thing that Tarantino, he made a movie actually before Reservoir Dogs that no one saw.
我读到塔伦蒂诺的这件事，他实际上在《落水狗》之前拍了一部没有人看过的电影。

00:48:24.347 --> 00:48:27.419
And he said, I made all my mistakes on that movie.
他说，我在那部电影中犯了所有的错误。

00:48:27.420 --> 00:48:28.500
I got all my mistakes out.
我把我所有的错误都改掉了。

00:48:28.500 --> 00:48:29.579
Like I figured out, what do I think?
就像我想的那样，我怎么想？

00:48:29.579 --> 00:48:30.420
I never knew that.
我从来不知道这一点。

00:48:30.420 --> 00:48:33.539
And he said to someone early on, like, I don't know what a light has seen.
他很早就对某人说过，我不知道光看到了什么。

00:48:33.539 --> 00:48:34.780
I don't know how to frame a shot.
我不知道如何构图。

00:48:34.780 --> 00:48:44.699
And they said, yeah, as an photographer does that, you just have to keep the story in mind and make sure that everything that's showing up on screen is in service to your vision of the story.
他们说，是的，作为一名摄影师，你只需牢记故事，并确保屏幕上显示的所有内容都服务于你对故事的看法。

00:48:44.699 --> 00:48:50.340
And I think Rob was an absolute master at, like you said, because you stack those all up against each other.
我认为罗布绝对是这方面的大师，就像你说的，因为你把这些都放在一起对比。

00:48:50.340 --> 00:48:55.059
You could probably isolate certain themes that recur.
您或许可以隔离某些重复出现的主题。

00:48:55.059 --> 00:49:11.179
You know, I mean, there is a notion of like true love, love wins the day, you know, the value in both friendship and also, and also seeing how friendship and how love evolves over time.
你知道，我的意思是，有一种像真爱一样的观念，爱情获胜，你知道，友谊和爱情的价值，以及友谊和爱情如何随着时间的推移而演变。

00:49:11.179 --> 00:49:21.260
When Harry Met Sally is astonishing the economy of storytelling, it almost could be a nine-year run of watching Harry and Sally find their way to each other, but he does it in two hours.
《当哈利遇见莎莉》的故事讲述成本惊人，几乎要花九年的时间看着哈利和莎莉找到彼此，但他只用了两个小时就完成了。

00:49:21.260 --> 00:49:22.260
There's no fat on it.
上面没有脂肪。

00:49:22.260 --> 00:49:24.980
It's just like, it's incredibly efficiently done.
就像，它完成得非常高效。

00:49:24.980 --> 00:49:27.099
Yeah, and that's part of his brilliance.
是的，这就是他的才华的一部分。

00:49:27.099 --> 00:49:31.860
It's just knowing what the story needs and not going past that, not never losing sight of that.
只是知道故事需要什么，而不是超越它，而不是永远忽视它。

00:49:31.860 --> 00:49:35.340
I know Carter, too, is just an enormous, enormous fan.
我知道卡特也是一个超级超级粉丝。

00:49:35.340 --> 00:49:48.059
And when we pitched the pilot, when we pitched Time With The Mother as a series, I guarantee you every time we pitched it, we referenced the Princess Bride and the future, and essentially Peter Fogg telling the story.
当我们推销试播集时，当我们推销《与母亲在一起的时光》系列时，我向你们保证，每次我们推销它时，我们都会提到公主新娘和未来，本质上是彼得·福格讲述的故事。

00:49:48.059 --> 00:49:52.019
I like, and when Harry Metzali, this is how we pitched the show.
我喜欢，当 Harry Metzali 时，这就是我们推销节目的方式。

00:49:52.019 --> 00:50:04.699
We pitched the show using Rob, And also the Princess Bride tells this kind of mythic fairy tale, but also narrator's head is pitching a kind of mythic fairy tale about his 20s and 30s in New York.
我们用罗伯来推销这个节目，《公主新娘》讲述了这种神话童话，而且叙述者的脑袋也在推销一种关于他20多岁和30多岁在纽约的神话童话。

00:50:04.699 --> 00:50:11.300
And Stan by me has that feeling too, like it's a fable, it's his writer's life, but it's how we all write our memories, right?
我身边的斯坦也有这种感觉，就像这是一个寓言，这是他作家的生活，但这就是我们所有人书写记忆的方式，对吗？

00:50:11.300 --> 00:50:13.099
We keep writing and refining our memories.
我们不断书写并完善我们的记忆。

00:50:13.099 --> 00:50:24.139
And I think he had, you know, you can see this from his dedication to politics, to free speech like he was an incredibly passionate man who also believed like we could be better.
我认为他，你知道，你可以从他对政治和言论自由的奉献中看到这一点，就像他是一个非常热情的人，也相信我们可以做得更好。

00:50:24.139 --> 00:50:25.139
Yes.
是的。

00:50:25.139 --> 00:50:29.219
You know, there was something in his movies that was aspirational in the best sense of the word.
你知道，他的电影中有一些东西是最好意义上的渴望的东西。

00:50:29.219 --> 00:50:37.820
I felt like even though you could definitely glean a through line of deep optimism, it was a hard-earned optimism, my favorite kind.
我觉得尽管你绝对可以收集到一系列深刻的乐观情绪，但这是一种来之不易的乐观情绪，是我最喜欢的一种。

00:50:37.820 --> 00:50:44.019
It was a realist's optimism, but it was definitely like there were headed someplace better.
这是一种现实主义者的乐观态度，但肯定会朝着更好的方向发展。

00:50:44.019 --> 00:50:45.019
Yes.
是的。

00:50:45.019 --> 00:50:48.519
Let's leave our characters better than we found them.
让我们让我们的角色比我们发现时更好。

00:50:48.519 --> 00:50:49.553
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

00:50:49.553 --> 00:50:50.299
That's right.
这是正确的。

00:50:50.299 --> 00:50:51.390
Let's let's evolve.
让我们一起进化吧。

00:50:51.390 --> 00:50:52.021
Let's grow.
让我们成长吧。

00:50:52.021 --> 00:50:55.637
And he was a curious kind of searching mind and heart that man.
他是一个具有好奇心和探索精神的人。

00:50:55.637 --> 00:50:58.679
It was so clear in his life and his work that we was.
他的生活和工作中的这一点与我们一样清晰。

00:50:58.679 --> 00:51:02.926
I didn't know that I didn't remember, I guess, that you acted in that pilot with him.
我不知道我不记得你和他一起演过那部试播集。

00:51:02.926 --> 00:51:03.775
He played my dad.
他扮演我的父亲。

00:51:03.775 --> 00:51:04.474
I forgot that.
我忘记了。

00:51:04.474 --> 00:51:06.722
I knew it was sort of him and he directed it.
我知道这是他干的，也是他导演的。

00:51:06.722 --> 00:51:08.620
I forgot you acted in scenes with him.
我忘了你和他一起演过戏。

00:51:08.620 --> 00:51:09.369
That's so cool.
太酷了。

00:51:09.369 --> 00:51:10.169
Yeah, of course.
是的，当然。

00:51:10.169 --> 00:51:14.015
It was the season right before how I made mothers that it was just the pilot.
那是在我让母亲们知道这只是试播集之前的一季。

00:51:14.015 --> 00:51:16.163
Just the pilot didn't get picked up by NBC.
只是试播集没有被 NBC 报道。

00:51:16.163 --> 00:51:19.960
But you got to act in scenes with with Rob Reiner who was also directing it.
但你必须和罗伯·莱纳一起演戏，他也是这部电影的导演。

00:51:19.960 --> 00:51:23.039
That's an incredible experience, man.
这是一次令人难以置信的经历，伙计。

00:51:23.039 --> 00:51:32.280
And I told this story in my Instagram post, but I'll just tell it to you now, but he was kind of behind the monitor and I was kind of lurking and talking to him a little bit.
我在 Instagram 帖子中讲述了这个故事，但我现在就告诉你，但他在监视器后面，而我则潜伏着并与他交谈了一会儿。

00:51:32.280 --> 00:51:35.570
And he turned to me and he said, I'm nervous.
他转向我说，我很紧张。

00:51:35.570 --> 00:51:37.809
And I said, you still get nervous?
我说，你还紧张吗？

00:51:37.809 --> 00:51:41.250
I thought like, why is he nervous for this pilot?
我想，为什么他对这位飞行员感到紧张？

00:51:41.250 --> 00:51:42.250
Have you seen?
你见过吗？

00:51:42.250 --> 00:51:48.289
And he said, if you're not nervous on the first day of shooting, it's time to leave the business, you know?
他说，如果你第一天拍摄不紧张，就该离开这个行业了，知道吗？

00:51:48.289 --> 00:51:50.250
Like nerves to him were a real sign.
对他来说，紧张是一个真实的迹象。

00:51:50.250 --> 00:51:52.090
You still cared so much.
你还是那么在乎。

00:51:52.090 --> 00:51:56.460
He still has seen it in the game and it was, his heart was in it.
他仍然在比赛中看到了这一点，而且他的心也在其中。

00:51:56.460 --> 00:51:59.460
His heart was in everything he did, including that.
他所做的一切都是他的心，包括那件事。

00:51:59.460 --> 00:52:01.300
It clings so deep into his career.
它深深地融入了他的职业生涯。

00:52:01.300 --> 00:52:02.900
He still was in it.
他仍然身在其中。

00:52:02.900 --> 00:52:04.860
I love that story and that says everything.
我喜欢这个故事，它说明了一切。

00:52:04.860 --> 00:52:05.739
Yeah, yeah.
是啊是啊。

00:52:05.739 --> 00:52:13.619
He just loved making things and he was a great collaborator and he was, he was truly, he offered himself as a mentor to me in a lot of ways.
他只是喜欢创造东西，他是一位出色的合作者，他确实在很多方面都成为了我的导师。

00:52:13.619 --> 00:52:23.219
You know, we, for a couple of years there, we were having lunch once a year or so And he was, you know, often with his producer, producing partner, Alan Greisman is a great guy who also produced that show.
你知道，我们在那里的几年里，我们每年大约吃一次午餐，你知道，他经常和他的制片人、制作伙伴一起吃午饭，艾伦·格雷斯曼是一个很棒的人，他也制作了那个节目。

00:52:24.260 --> 00:52:25.780
And they were just really kind to me.
他们对我真的很好。

00:52:25.780 --> 00:52:30.659
And I'll never forget him inviting me over to the house to screen the cut of liberal arts.
我永远不会忘记他邀请我去家里放映文科剪辑。

00:52:30.659 --> 00:52:38.699
And he cast me in that pilot when I was, I don't know, 28, 29, 27, maybe, I don't know.
当我，我不知道，28岁、29岁、27岁，也许，我不知道的时候，他让我出演那个试播集。

00:52:38.699 --> 00:52:41.420
But I was a couple of years out of grad school.
但我已经毕业几年了。

00:52:41.420 --> 00:52:46.219
I think I had been on Broadway in the graduate and I'd gotten fired from my first pilot.
我想我毕业时曾在百老汇演出，但我被我的第一个飞行员解雇了。

00:52:46.219 --> 00:52:47.940
The second series didn't work.
第二个系列没有成功。

00:52:47.940 --> 00:52:51.780
The third pilot season, I tested like 10 times and didn't get anything.
第三个试播季，我测试了大约10次，但什么也没得到。

00:52:51.780 --> 00:52:55.340
And so this was like my fourth pilot season, maybe fifth pilot season.
这就像我的第四个试播季，也许是第五个试播季。

00:52:55.340 --> 00:53:09.190
And I don't know, just to be able to like, there are these moments, like maybe you felt this way about Letterman, Craig, but where, when you tell your parents who cast you or what you're doing, they get it.
我不知道，只是为了能够喜欢，有这些时刻，就像你可能对莱特曼、克雷格有这样的感觉，但是当你告诉你的父母是谁选了你或者你在做什么时，他们就会明白。

00:53:09.190 --> 00:53:12.409
Like your parents in Long Island, your parents in Ohio, they get it.
就像你在长岛的父母、你在俄亥俄州的父母一样，他们明白这一点。

00:53:12.409 --> 00:53:16.949
Like my parents grew up watching all in the, you know, they watched all in the family.
就像我的父母从小就看着一切，你知道，他们看着家里的一切。

00:53:16.949 --> 00:53:18.610
They watched and loved all those movies.
他们观看并喜爱所有这些电影。

00:53:18.610 --> 00:53:31.429
So when I got to say Rob Reiner cast me in a pilot for NBC, they also knew what NBC was, there was something that that we, it was important moment for me.
所以当我说 Rob Reiner 让我出演 NBC 的试播集时，他们也知道 NBC 是什么，我们有一些东西，这对我来说是重要的时刻。

00:53:31.429 --> 00:53:32.949
It's important, I know what you mean.
这很重要，我知道你的意思。

00:53:32.949 --> 00:53:34.230
It's important.
这很重要。

00:53:34.230 --> 00:53:35.429
I have a real job.
我有一份真正的工作。

00:53:35.429 --> 00:53:37.829
I'm really doing this because this person believes in me.
我这样做真的是因为这个人相信我。

00:53:37.829 --> 00:53:43.750
Yeah, and I remember I shot the pilot and my grandfather died before I got the news.
是的，我记得我射杀了飞行员，在我得知消息之前我的祖父就去世了。

00:53:43.750 --> 00:53:44.789
I actually got the news.
我确实得到了消息。

00:53:44.789 --> 00:53:49.550
It wasn't picked up the day of my grandfather's funeral, but my dad said something really kind of sweet.
我祖父葬礼那天没有收到，但我父亲说了一些非常甜蜜的话。

00:53:49.550 --> 00:53:58.630
He said, well, your grandpa went to his death thinking you were doing a show for NBC with Rob Reiner, like, that's okay, that's okay.
他说，好吧，你爷爷去世时还以为你在和 Rob Reiner 一起为 NBC 做节目，就像，没关系，没关系。

00:53:58.630 --> 00:54:01.269
That was good for him to feel into that.
能够感受到这一点对他来说是件好事。

00:54:01.269 --> 00:54:12.760
And it was just like, there are these moments, maybe we've talked about this, but there are these moments as an artist, as a young actor or writer where you lose faith in yourself.
就像，有些时刻，也许我们已经讨论过这一点，但作为一名艺术家、一名年轻演员或作家，有些时刻你会对自己失去信心。

00:54:12.760 --> 00:54:13.547
it's natural.
这是自然的。

00:54:13.547 --> 00:54:15.425
Is this going to happen for me?
这会发生在我身上吗？

00:54:15.425 --> 00:54:17.364
Oh, it's happening for that guy.
哦，这件事发生在那个人身上。

00:54:17.364 --> 00:54:19.605
Why isn't it happening for me or her?
为什么这不会发生在我或她身上？

00:54:19.605 --> 00:54:24.088
And then there are these people that come along and say, hey, we need you.
然后有些人走过来说，嘿，我们需要你。

00:54:24.088 --> 00:54:24.936
We'd like you.
我们想要你。

00:54:24.936 --> 00:54:25.845
You're the guy.
你就是那个家伙。

00:54:25.845 --> 00:54:27.298
You're the one for this.
你就是这个人。

00:54:27.298 --> 00:54:32.145
And Rob came along at a moment that I needed someone to believe in me, like him.
当我需要有人像他一样相信我时，罗布出现了。

00:54:32.145 --> 00:54:33.356
I needed Rob Reiner.
我需要罗布·莱纳。

00:54:33.356 --> 00:54:36.082
It was great that it was actually Rob Reiner.
很高兴这实际上是罗布·莱纳。

00:54:36.082 --> 00:54:39.960
I got the actual guy to say, and I remember auditioning for him.
我有一个真正的人要说，我记得为他试镜。

00:54:39.960 --> 00:54:41.599
and I remember making him laugh.
我记得让他笑了。

00:54:41.599 --> 00:54:59.079
I remember there was a great, funny comedian actress who played my wife, Mary Gallagher, and we were improvising at the, I think at the network, like it was our network test, and he was kind of interviewing us, and maybe he was playing the couples therapist essentially, like we were in couples therapy.
我记得有一位伟大、有趣的喜剧女演员扮演我的妻子玛丽·加拉格尔，我们在网络上即兴创作，就像我们的网络测试一样，他在采访我们，也许他本质上是在扮演夫妻治疗师，就像我们在夫妻治疗中一样。

00:54:59.079 --> 00:55:04.599
And she was like, I don't wanna do anything crazy fancy for the wedding, you know?
她说，我不想为婚礼做任何疯狂的事情，你知道吗？

00:55:04.599 --> 00:55:07.000
And she wanted this like kind of hippie wedding.
她想要一场类似嬉皮士的婚礼。

00:55:07.000 --> 00:55:11.760
And I was like, my mom, my parents are not gonna, like, and they're like, well, where do you want to get married?
我当时想，我的妈妈，我的父母不会，他们会说，好吧，你想在哪里结婚？

00:55:11.760 --> 00:55:17.000
And I was like, Chippurianis, which is like the most fancy place you could get married in New York City.
我当时想，Chippurianis，这是纽约市最高档的结婚地点。

00:55:17.000 --> 00:55:21.079
Like, it's like, you know, it's absurd how aristocratic it is.
就像，就像，你知道，它是多么的贵族化，这是荒谬的。

00:55:21.440 --> 00:55:27.920
But I knew, I knew Chippurianis because I think like an ex girlfriend's friend had gotten married there.
但我知道，我认识奇普里亚尼斯，因为我觉得就像前女友的朋友在那里结婚了一样。

00:55:28.119 --> 00:55:33.840
But Rob knew Chippurianis and he almost fell out of his seat, you know, it was like the perfect thing.
但罗布认识奇普里亚尼斯，他差点从座位上摔下来，你知道，这就像是一件完美的事情。

00:55:33.840 --> 00:55:36.400
I think it got me the job that I knew.
我认为它让我得到了我所熟悉的工作。

00:55:36.400 --> 00:55:40.400
I can't imagine the satisfaction of knowing you made a murder.
我无法想象知道你犯了谋杀罪后的满足感。

00:55:40.400 --> 00:55:41.400
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:41.400 --> 00:55:42.400
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:42.400 --> 00:55:43.400
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:43.400 --> 00:55:44.400
Like really laugh.
真的很喜欢笑。

00:55:44.400 --> 00:55:45.400
Like what?
比如什么？

00:55:45.400 --> 00:55:46.400
That's, that's, you'll always have that moment.
就是这样，就是这样，你永远都会有那一刻。

00:55:46.400 --> 00:55:47.400
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:47.400 --> 00:55:48.400
That's amazing.
太棒了。

00:55:48.400 --> 00:55:51.400
And he was also, he was also, um, you know, some funny people don't laugh.
他也是，他也是，嗯，你知道，一些有趣的人不会笑。

00:55:51.400 --> 00:55:52.400
Yes.
是的。

00:55:52.400 --> 00:55:53.400
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:55:53.400 --> 00:55:54.400
Oh, he was a funny person who laughed.
哦，他是一个爱笑的有趣的人。

00:55:54.400 --> 00:55:55.400
So you fell.
于是你就摔倒了。

00:55:55.400 --> 00:55:56.400
I know.
我知道。

00:55:56.400 --> 00:55:57.400
He's so well.
他很好。

00:55:57.400 --> 00:55:58.400
He felt his work and felt his generosity.
他感受到了他的工作，感受到了他的慷慨。

00:55:58.400 --> 00:56:00.400
I also felt him wanting us to do well.
我也感觉到他希望我们表现出色。

00:56:00.400 --> 00:56:01.400
We were clearly the ones he want.
我们显然是他想要的人。

00:56:01.400 --> 00:56:02.400
I think we were there.
我想我们就在那里。

00:56:02.400 --> 00:56:03.400
We were the only ones who tested.
我们是唯一进行测试的人。

00:56:03.400 --> 00:56:04.400
Like he wanted it to be us.
就像他希望是我们一样。

00:56:04.400 --> 00:56:04.900
us.
我们。

00:56:04.900 --> 00:56:07.975
He created an environment where we could do our best work.
他创造了一个让我们可以尽最大努力工作的环境。

00:56:07.975 --> 00:56:10.414
So, you know, it's also, it's a strange thing.
所以，你知道，这也是一件奇怪的事情。

00:56:10.414 --> 00:56:11.846
I made this thing with him.
我和他一起做了这件事。

00:56:11.846 --> 00:56:13.860
We worked together for a couple weeks.
我们一起工作了几个星期。

00:56:13.519 --> 00:56:17.840
No one ended up seeing it except some NBC executives who said we're going to pass on this.
除了一些 NBC 高管表示我们将转达这一消息外，最终没有人看到它。

00:56:17.840 --> 00:56:21.875
So it's not like I have this big document of like, this is what we made together.
所以我没有这么大的文件，这是我们一起制作的。

00:56:21.875 --> 00:56:28.352
I think I saw one cut of it or something and it was like, I'm just moved on and then I did how I met your mother in the next year.
我想我看到了其中的一个片段或其他东西，就像，我只是继续前进，然后我做了第二年遇见你母亲的事情。

00:56:28.352 --> 00:56:34.679
But yeah, I am forever grateful that he, he said, he pointed and said, you, I'm I'm grateful I got to spend some time with him.
但是，是的，我永远感激他，他说，他指着说，你，我很感激我能和他一起度过一些时间。

00:56:34.679 --> 00:56:42.599
I'm grateful for those lunches and I'm grateful that those movies live on and inspired us and inspired people even that didn't know him.
我很感激这些午餐，我很感激这些电影一直存在，激励着我们，激励着那些不认识他的人。

